# "nedelja" names both the weekday Sunday and, in some sources, the week
# (see weekday_6.voc) -- a COUNT immediately before it ("dve nedelja", "10
# nedelja") can only be a span of weeks, since nobody counts specific
# Sundays that way, but this locale ships no week duration unit under
# "nedelja" (sedmica is the unambiguous week word; unit_week.voc/
# unit1_week.voc). Answering the lone-Sunday sub-reading and stranding the
# count would be a worse wrong answer than none, so the count vetoes the
# weekday match instead of asserting the unsourced week reading. Wiktionary,
# nedelja -- https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nedelja#Serbo-Croatian
nedelja
недеља
# "nedelje" is the paucal (2-4) GENITIVE SINGULAR of the same noun --
# unit_week.voc's own "sedmica"/"sedmice" pair uses that exact case for a
# counted week ("dve sedmice"), so "dve nedelje" is read the same way and
# needs the same veto the nominative gets above. Wiktionary, nedelja,
# declension table -- https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nedelja#Serbo-Croatian
nedelje
недеље
